    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d673">

                <pb facs="0659" n="653" sameAs="frus:frus1894app1/pg653"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wharton to Baron Ketteler.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-10-19"><hi rendition="#italic">October 19,
                        1892</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge, with
                    thanks, the receipt of your note of the 7th instant, inclosing a memorandum
                    relative to the views of the Imperial German Government in regard to a
                    difference of opinion which has recently arisen between the consular board and
                    the municipal council at Apia with regard to the appointment of returning
                    officers for municipal elections.</p>
                <p>Accept, sir, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William F. Wharton</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
